# ============================================================
# PETALYX — HOP C (lexx3_listen.py)
# CGL-MESSAGING-PROTOCOL-001 v1.0 §4
#
# These two values are read ONLY by api/petalyx-*.js, which run
# server-side. Neither may ever appear in a file that reaches a
# browser, and neither is ever echoed in a response body.
#
# Local:  copy this file to .env and put the real values in it.
# Deploy: set them in the Vercel project (Settings -> Environment
#         Variables), not in the repo.
#
# Both placeholders below are deliberately invalid. With either one
# unset or left as-is, every /api/petalyx-* endpoint answers
# 503 { "error": "widget_not_configured" } and logs which is missing.
# ============================================================

# The externally-reachable base URL of lexx3_listen.py. No trailing
# slash, no path — the endpoint paths are appended by the proxy:
#   {base}/petalyx/session/initiate
#   {base}/petalyx/session/{session_token}/response
#   {base}/petalyx/session/{session_token}/abandon
#
# PENDING FROM ANDREW. Port 8300 is confirmed as the port
# lexx3_listen.py binds internally on the droplet; what is reachable
# from outside it is NOT confirmed and must not be guessed. It could
# be the same IP on a different port, or a different host entirely.
PETALYX_BASE_URL=

# The X-Widget-Key issued for the Petalyx UI.
#
# PENDING FROM ANDREW. This is NOT the X-Gateway-Key: that one belongs
# to Hop A/B (h1_gateway.py, port 8100, server-to-server, numeric) and
# Petalyx must never hold it. If a value here starts getting 401s,
# check first that it is the widget key and not the gateway key.
PETALYX_WIDGET_KEY=
